    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0404" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/123</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary General of the High Commission for
                        Refugees</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jewish and Other</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Coming From Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wurfbain</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d246-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lausanne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-04">April 4, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg herewith to refer to my letter of
                    March 22nd.,<anchor n="5a" xml:id="d246-f2"/> and to take the liberty of drawing
                    your attention to the fact that the communications addressed by this office to
                    your Government on February 6th. and 21st.,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d246-f3"/>
                    concerning especially the question of passports for refugees from Germany and
                    that of the treatment of stateless refugees, have so far remained without answer
                    on the part of the Government of the United States of America.</p>
                <p>As the above-mentioned questions are again to figure on the agenda of the next
                    meeting of the Governing Body of the High Commission, it would be highly
                    appreciated by this office if your Government would <pb facs="0405" n="305"
                        xml:id="pg305"/> kindly inform the High Commissioner before that meeting of
                    the attitude it intends to adopt with regard to the afore-mentioned
                    recommendations.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wurfbain</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d246-f1" n="6" type="source" xml:id="d246-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to the Department by the Consul at Geneva in his despatch No. 869
                    Political, April 6; received April 21.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d246-f2" n="5a" xml:id="d246-f2-content">
